  </knowledge>
  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Extend EmailDraftToolHandler with draft_reply(communicationId, mode) and draft_forward(communicationId) that auto-generate the authored body region (the part 024's bodyOverride injects above the quoted thread).</step>
    <step order="2">Add summarize_thread(communicationId): load the .eml via eml-render (FileAccessEndpoints.cs:901) / document-context, then reuse the existing file/document-summarize prompt/response path to answer in chat with a plain narrative.</step>
    <step order="3">Register the three tools as ADR-039 catalog rows via the Services/Ai/PublicContracts/ facade — no fork.</step>
    <step order="4">Verify summarize_thread output matches the file-summarize shape (plain narrative, no bespoke format) and opens no composer.</step>
    <step order="5">Add/extend unit tests in tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ (auto-draft body produced; summarize_thread narrative shape; OBO/id-fetch; no prompt content).</step>
    <step order="6">dotnet build + dotnet publish size check; record absolute + delta; run the vulnerable-package scan.</step>
    <step order="7">Update TASK-INDEX ✅.</step>
  </steps>
  <escalation>
    <trigger>If reaching parity with the file/document-summarize output requires anything beyond reusing that handler's prompt/response path over the .eml (i.e. a bespoke thread-summary format seems necessary), STOP and escalate (FR-09 resolved: identical to file summarize) rather than inventing a format.</trigger>
  </escalation>
  <justification>
    <existing>EmailDraftToolHandler exists; IRagService/DocumentContextService + eml-render (FileAccessEndpoints.cs:901) and the file/document-summarize path exist.</existing>
    <extension>Extend EmailDraftToolHandler with three tools; reuse the file-summarize path over the .eml — no new handler family, no new summarize format.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Reply/Forward cards cannot auto-draft and "Summarize the thread" has no backing — the per-item Email DoD (FR-09/FR-10) fails.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>
  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/** EmailDraftToolHandler (extended with draft_reply/draft_forward/summarize_thread)</output>
    <output type="code">the ADR-039 catalog rows registering the three tools</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ email per-item tool unit tests</output>
  </outputs>
  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">draft_reply(communicationId, mode) and draft_forward(communicationId) auto-generate an authored body region (the input 024's bodyOverride injects).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">summarize_thread(communicationId) loads the .eml via eml-render/document-context and answers in chat.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">summarize_thread output is a plain narrative IDENTICAL in form to the existing file/document-summarize handler — not a bespoke structured format (negative case).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">summarize_thread opens NO composer.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The tools live on an EXTENSION of EmailDraftToolHandler — no new handler family (negative case).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Content is fetched by communicationId over OBO; no email content enters the prompt (ADR-015).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Publish size ≤60 MB reported (absolute + delta); no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Unit tests added/updated in tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ and pass.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
  <notes>The draft_* tools produce the body that task 024's `bodyOverride` injects (composes above the quoted thread — the thread-preservation invariant, FR-10). Coordinate with redesign-r2 (Services/Ai internals, PublicContracts no fork) and email-r5 (email handler); /conflict-check before the PR.</notes>
